---
layout: base.njk
title: "Browse indicators"
description: "Every indicator this site holds, by type: email addresses, IP addresses, GitHub and LinkedIn accounts, wallets, packages and file hashes reported in connection with North Korean (DPRK) cyber operations, each with its own page."
permalink: "/indicators/browse/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
  src/indicators/browse-index.njk — the directory of the browse listing

  Links to every page of every per-type run cut by browseRuns() in
  src/_data/iocIndex.js; src/indicators/browse.njk renders the runs. /indicators/,
  which the home page links to, lists the types and links here, so any
  indicator page is at most four clicks from the home page. This URL is the one the
  rest of the site links to as "Browse indicators".
#}
<section>
  <h1>Browse indicators</h1>
  <p>
    Every indicator this site holds, {{ iocIndex.totals.all | thousands }} in
    all, listed by type and then by value. Each value links to its own page,
    which carries every source that reported it and the text around it. To look
    up one value, the search on <a href="/remote-workers/">Remote Workers</a> is
    faster.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Indicators</th><th scope="col">Pages</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for entry in iocIndex.indicator_browse_types %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.kind.plural }}</a></th>
          <td>{{ entry.total | thousands }}</td>
          <td>{% for run in entry.runs %}<a href="{{ run.url }}" aria-label="{{ entry.kind.plural }}, page {{ run.number }}">{{ run.number }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>
<section>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Disclaimer",
    preset: "not-proof",
    body: 'Compromised packages and repositories name victims. See the <a href="/sources/#sourcing-methodology">sourcing methodology</a>.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>
